.TH BENEDICT 1 "2026-09-21" "benedict 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
benedict \- push-to-talk ChatGPT dictation for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B benedict
.I COMMAND
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B benedict
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B benedict
lets you dictate into any application.
Hold the hotkey
.RB ( RightCtrl+Space
by default), speak, and release.
The transcript is inserted at the cursor of the focused window.
.PP
Speech recognition is performed by ChatGPT's web dictation, driven through a
hidden Chrome instance running under Xvfb.
The instance stays signed in to your own ChatGPT account, so no API key or
extra credits are required.
A floating status pill and desktop notifications show the live state, the
active microphone, and the transcript as it forms.
.PP
Run
.B benedict
without arguments to list the available commands.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Run the dictation daemon in the foreground.
This is what the
.B benedict
systemd user service executes; you rarely need to start it by hand.
.TP
.B login
Open a visible Chrome window so you can sign in to ChatGPT once.
Use
.B \-\-import
to copy an existing ChatGPT session from another browser instead of signing
in again.
.TP
.B probe
Dump the ChatGPT page controls that
.B benedict
looks for.
Useful when OpenAI changes the web UI and the selectors need updating.
.TP
.B doctor
Check system prerequisites such as packages, services, input access, and the
GNOME extension, and print a pass/fail checklist.
Exits non-zero if any check fails.
.TP
.B config
Print the effective settings and the path to the configuration file.
.TP
.B pill
Play a short demonstration of every status-pill state.
.TP
.B last
Print the most recent transcript.
.TP
.B status
Print the daemon's current state as JSON.
.TP
.B test\-hotkey
Wait for the hotkey chord and report press and release events.
Use this to verify that keyd is delivering the chord.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Global
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help for
.B benedict
or for a given command and exit.
.SS login
.TP
.B \-\-import
Import the ChatGPT session from an existing Chrome, Brave, Chromium, Edge, or
Vivaldi profile.
.TP
.B \-\-browser " " \fIBROWSER\fR
Source browser to import from:
.IR brave ", " chrome ", " chromium ", " edge ", or " vivaldi .
.SS doctor
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colored output.
.SS config
.TP
.B \-\-edit
Open the configuration file in
.BR $EDITOR ,
creating it from the defaults if it does not exist.
.SS pill
.TP
.B \-\-position " " \fIPOSITION\fR
Override the pill position for the demo:
.IR bottom-center ", " bottom-right ", " top-center ", or " top-right .
.TP
.B \-\-force
Run the demo even if the daemon looks busy.
.SS test\-hotkey
.TP
.B \-\-seconds " " \fISECONDS\fR
How long to listen for the chord (default: 10).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/benedict/config.toml
User configuration.
All keys are optional.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/benedict/
Daemon state, logs, the last transcript, and the transcript history.
.TP
.I /etc/keyd/default.conf
keyd configuration that maps the hotkey chord to F24.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EDITOR
Editor used by
.BR "benedict config \-\-edit" .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, disables colored output, as if
.B \-\-no\-color
were passed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B benedict doctor
Verify that everything is installed and working.
.TP
.B benedict login \-\-import
Sign in to ChatGPT by copying the session from your everyday browser.
.TP
.B systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now ydotoold benedict
Enable and start the background services.
.TP
.B benedict test\-hotkey
Confirm the hotkey chord is being delivered.
.TP
.B journalctl \-\-user \-u benedict \-f
Follow the daemon log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR keyd (1)
.PP
Full documentation: https://github.com/Anikate-De/benedict
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/Anikate-De/benedict/issues
.PP
.B benedict
is not affiliated with OpenAI, and it may break when the ChatGPT web UI or
usage limits change.
